 "notes": "Red 'Auriga' curve of Fig. 5 (e-print file DMplotZOOM.png), digitised from pixel positions calibrated on the axis ticks (bottom mass axis linear 3.0-4.5e-12 eV, log y with 67 px/decade). The paper sets identical 95% C.L. upper limits on the dimensionless dilaton couplings d_i for both an electromagnetic gauge modulus (d_i=d_e) and an electron-mass modulus (d_i=d_me); the abstract quotes d_e ~< 1e-5 near m_phi=3.6e-12 eV, so ScalarPhoton is reported here, but the same curve applies verbatim to d_me (ScalarElectron). Paper convention alpha = alpha0[1 + d_e sqrt(4 pi G_N) Phi] (eq. 2) is exactly the canonical Damour-Donoghue kappa=sqrt(4pi)/M_Pl normalisation, so no conversion applied. Curve spans 850.7-948.6 Hz (m=3.52e-12 to 3.92e-12 eV), matching the stated AURIGA sensitive band [850,950] Hz; dips to ~3e-6 at the detector normal modes (~868 and ~929 Hz). Standard halo model with rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3 assumed.",
